@@ -261,7 +261,7 @@ A parked call binds to its callback by **tool name and phase** — the same iden
 
 - Editing a callback body (or anything else that does not change tool names) is safe: replaying a parked call runs the latest deployed code with the closure values snapshotted when the call was made.
 - If a persisted callback has no registered implementation (fresh process after a crash, or after a redeploy), eve re-runs `session.started` resolvers once to rebind it, then replays.
-- If the tool no longer exists under that name, replay fails closed with an explicit error instead of invoking something else. Ordinary turn-scoped and step-scoped tools are not rebound; a parked call to a missing one errors. Framework-provided resolvers such as memory provider-tool wrappers opt into the same generic missing-callback rebind while preserving their locked scope.
+- If the tool no longer exists under that name, replay fails closed with an explicit error instead of invoking something else. Ordinary turn-scoped and step-scoped tools are not rebound by default; a parked call to a missing one errors. An idempotent turn-scoped tool resolver can opt in with `defineDynamic({ rebindMissingCallbacks: true, events: { ... } })`. Recovery may run that resolver again to register callback implementations; keep I/O read-only and do not perform external actions in it. Persisted callback closures and tool identity remain locked to the original call. Step-scoped callbacks are not covered by this option. Framework-provided resolvers such as memory provider-tool wrappers opt into the same generic missing-callback rebind while preserving their locked scope.
 
